OL,3,AGovernment could force media industry
OL,4,Ato improve safeguards after Walliams
OL,5,Aallegations
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe government is prepared to force the
OL,8,Fentertainment industry to improve
OL,9,Fsafeguarding practices unless rapid
OL,10,Fchange is introduced, BBC Newsnight has
OL,11,Flearned.
OL,13,FAn investigation by the Guardian and
OL,14,FITV News alleged that entertainer David
OL,15,FWalliams had been accused by several
OL,16,Fwomen of sexual misconduct and abusing
OL,17,Fhis position, which he denies.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
PN,16102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F161A1794466454
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AGovernment could force media industry
OL,4,Ato improve safeguards after Walliams
OL,5,Aallegations
OL,6,
OL,7,FCulture Secretary Lisa Nandy will tell
OL,8,Fa meeting of industry leaders next week
OL,9,Fthat if their response to recent
OL,10,Fallegations is not robust enough, she
OL,11,Fis prepared to force participation in
OL,12,Fthe industry body to protect
OL,13,Fwhistleblowers, the BBC understands.
OL,15,FParticipation in the Creative
OL,16,FIndustries Independent Standards
OL,17,FAuthority (CIISA) is currently
OL,18,Fvoluntary.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
